1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
NEXUS connects engineering knowledge to support accountable product decisions.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:20,000
The landing page brings registered vocabularies and business information into one workspace.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:37,000
The industrial foundation preserves shared meaning across parts, designs, requirements and activities.

4
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Customer terminology remains connected to its original source.

5
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Select the intended part and source version before investigating a change.

6
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:15,000
The agent retrieves recorded dependencies and retains its findings for review.

7
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Assembly and manufacturing process records provide context for the change review.

8
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Missing revision, configuration and effectivity information remains visible.

9
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:53,000
Similarity ranks reuse candidates and exposes missing engineering properties.

10
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Recorded parent assemblies help specialists trace a component change backward.

11
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Short-term, long-term and contextual memory each support a different kind of continuity.

12
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Short-term continuity lets an engineer ask a follow-up without repeating the entire product story.

13
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:37,000
The PMI answer retains the housing context and returns the recorded tolerance and datum.

14
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:52,000
Long-term recall reopens retained conversation evidence after a reload.

15
00:02:52,000 --> 00:03:07,000
A saved answer is historical evidence, so its freshness still requires checking.

16
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Contextual memory binds the discussion to the selected business identity and ontology scope.

17
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Conversation persistence does not establish automatic training or an approved engineering lesson.

18
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:48,000
The graph connects the housing to recorded CAD, MBSE, requirement, assembly, manufacturing and quality information.

19
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:58,000
A requirement question focuses the graph on the cited housing and requirement records.

20
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:13,000
A PMI follow-up changes the visualization to the recorded housing and bore-tolerance association.

21
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:28,000
The recorded PMI value is 0.02 millimetres with datum A.

22
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:40,000
Restore the broader context to explore the selected part and its supporting records.

23
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Where Used traces backward from the housing to its recorded parent assembly.

24
00:04:52,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Recorded paths support investigation without proving complete lifecycle coverage or requirement satisfaction.

25
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:10,000
The Governor coordinates the Teamcenter PLMXML and AP242 merge plan and its matching tools.

26
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:20,000
The Steward checks governance and validation evidence before publication can proceed.

27
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Inspect each proposed pair using its definitions, labels, property context and character trigrams.

28
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:40,000
The combined similarity score ranks candidates for review and does not prove semantic equivalence.

29
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:50,000
Validation is still pending in this recorded plan, so approval remains blocked.

30
00:05:50,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Neither original ontology is replaced, and no consolidation or publication is approved by this demonstration.

31
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:10,000
Catalog search finds retained engineering sources and their import history.

32
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:20,000
Registered sources remain separate from approved, published data products.

33
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:30,000
Data Products guides source selection, analysis configuration and workflow review.

34
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:40,000
Preparation and release approval remain distinct steps before data is shared.

35
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:50,000
Metadata Registry provides source-scoped vocabulary, definitions and ownership information.

36
00:06:50,000 --> 00:07:00,000
Filter Teamcenter terms to inspect their meaning before preparing a governed draft.
